Rockbox STM32U5A5 Duro Port
============================

This is a Rockbox port for the STM32U5A5-based Duro audio player device.

Project Structure
=================

The port is organized as follows:

firmware/target/arm/stm32u5/
  ├── cpu-stm32u5a5.h          - CPU header with memory layout
  ├── stm32u5a5.h              - STM32U5A5 register definitions
  ├── clock-stm32u5.h          - Clock structures and definitions
  ├── duro/                     - Device-specific code
  │   ├── clock-duro.{c,h}     - Clock initialization
  │   ├── system-duro.{c,h}    - System configuration
  │   ├── lcd-duro.{c,h}       - LCD/display driver
  │   ├── i2c-duro.{c,h}       - I2C bus support
  │   ├── button-duro.{c,h}    - Button/keypad driver
  │   ├── backlight-duro.{c,h} - Backlight control
  │   ├── audiohw-duro.{c,h}   - Audio hardware
  │   ├── pcm-duro.{c,h}       - PCM audio streaming
  │   ├── sdmmc-duro.{c,h}     - SD/MMC card support
  │   └── usb-duro.{c,h}       - USB support
  ├── {gpio,i2c,sdmmc,spi,system,timer,usb,debug}-stm32u5.c
  └── crt0-stm32u5.S, vectors-stm32u5.S - Startup code

firmware/export/
  ├── config/duro.h            - Duro configuration header
  ├── stm32u5A5-config.h       - STM32U5 architecture config

bootloader/
  └── duro.c                   - Duro bootloader

apps/keymaps/
  └── keymap-duro.c            - Button mappings

Key Features
============

1. CPU: STM32U5A5 (ARM Cortex-M33, 160 MHz max)
2. Memory: 2.5 MB SRAM
3. Display: 480x360 RGB565 TFT LCD via LTDC
4. Audio: SAI1 audio interface, supports AIC3x codec
5. Storage: SD/MMC card via SDMMC1
6. USB: USB OTG High-Speed or Full-Speed
7. Input: Power, Hold, Volume up/down buttons
8. Power: Battery monitoring with charging

Build Instructions
==================

To build the Duro port:

    ./tools/configure
    # Select option 271 (Duro)
    make

Bootloader:
    make bootloader

