Configuration Notes
===================

The Duro configuration is set in firmware/export/config/duro.h:

- Display: 480x360 pixels, RGB565 (16-bit)
- Audio: 44.1 kHz default sample rate
- Plugin buffer: 1 MB
- Codec buffer: 512 KB
- RTC: STM32U5 internal RTC
- USB IDs: VID=0x6666, PID=0xDU50

Clock Configuration
===================

The STM32U5A5 supports multiple clock sources:
- HSI: 16 MHz internal oscillator
- HSE: External oscillator (16-24 MHz typical)
- PLL1: Main system clock (up to 160 MHz)
- PLL2: Audio clock
- PLL3: Peripheral clocks
- LSI: 32 kHz low-speed oscillator
- LSE: 32.768 kHz RTC oscillator (external)

The current framework uses:
- HSI as primary clock source
- PLL1Q for SDMMC (160 MHz)
- PLL3R for LTDC/LCD (40 MHz typical)
- SAI1 for audio interface

Hardware Integration Notes
===========================

1. GPIO Configuration:
   - Power button: GPIOF[0]
   - Hold button: GPIOF[1]
   - Volume up: GPIOG[0]
   - Volume down: GPIOG[1]
   (Adjust in button-duro.h based on actual schematic)

2. I2C Devices:
   - Audio codec: 0x18
   - PMIC: 0x6A
   - Touch controller: 0x2C
   (Configure in i2c-duro.h)

3. Audio:
   - Codec: AIC34xx family
   - Interface: SAI1 (Serial Audio Interface)
   - Sample rates: 44.1 kHz, 48 kHz (configurable)

4. Display:
   - Interface: LTDC (LCD-TFT Display Controller)
   - Resolution: 480x360 @ 16-bit RGB565
   - Framebuffer: SRAM-based

Development Tips
================

1. Use the debugger to verify clock initialization:
   - Check RCC register values
   - Verify PLL lock status
   - Confirm bus clock frequencies

2. Test peripheral initialization in order:
   - Clocks
   - GPIO
   - I2C (codec communication)
   - Display
   - Audio
   - Storage

3. Reference Implementation:
   - See firmware/target/arm/stm32/echoplayer/ for H7 reference
   - STM32U5 datasheet for register definitions
   - This port's header files for required APIs

Troubleshooting
===============

If the device doesn't boot:
1. Check clock configuration (verify PLL lock)
2. Verify GPIO pin assignments
3. Check bootloader addresses in linker script
4. Ensure stack pointer is correctly initialized

If USB doesn't work:
1. Verify OTG PHY configuration
2. Check USB clock source
3. Confirm USB device descriptors

If audio doesn't play:
1. Verify I2C codec communication
2. Check SAI clock and pin configuration
3. Confirm DMA setup for audio buffers

